1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,587
This year I invested in chip
stocks and lost 250,000,000 won,

2
00:00:04,587 --> 00:00:06,414
70% of everything I owned.

3
00:00:06,794 --> 00:00:10,802
I borrowed too, and the July
crash force-sold my loan first.

4
00:00:11,182 --> 00:00:12,904
I'm forty-four, my job is shaky,

5
00:00:12,904 --> 00:00:16,187
and my daughter's private tutoring
academy fees come monthly.

6
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:18,761
I have 100,000,000 won
left for retirement,

7
00:00:18,761 --> 00:00:20,394
and I haven't even told my wife.

8
00:00:20,774 --> 00:00:22,601
I thought I should quit stocks.

9
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:25,354
But just as it isn't a
loss unless you sell,

10
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:28,924
I figured it wasn't a real loss yet as
long as I stayed in the stock market.

11
00:00:29,304 --> 00:00:32,418
So to win back my principal,
I decided to study properly,

12
00:00:32,418 --> 00:00:34,384
and I looked into 5 rules to follow.

13
00:00:35,384 --> 00:00:38,293
First, move from Korean
stocks to US stocks.

14
00:00:38,673 --> 00:00:41,808
"Gukjang" means Korean
stocks, "mijang" US stocks.

15
00:00:42,188 --> 00:00:44,678
Many retail "ants" buy only Korean stocks.

16
00:00:45,058 --> 00:00:47,154
But KOSPI, Korea's main stock index,

17
00:00:47,154 --> 00:00:50,998
is now over half Samsung Electronics
and SK hynix by market value.

18
00:00:51,378 --> 00:00:55,437
So buying KOSPI basically means going
all-in on one industry: semiconductors.

19
00:00:55,817 --> 00:00:58,661
And even there, I put money
only in semiconductors.

20
00:00:59,041 --> 00:01:02,511
So when chips wobble, the
whole market wobbles with them.

21
00:01:02,891 --> 00:01:08,596
On July 13, KOSPI fell 8.95% in one day,
and trading even halted for 20 minutes.

22
00:01:08,976 --> 00:01:12,486
Then in all of July,
it fell more than 34%.

23
00:01:12,866 --> 00:01:16,795
Holding only chips like
me, I took the full hit.

24
00:01:17,175 --> 00:01:18,483
Long term, same story.

25
00:01:18,863 --> 00:01:24,540
KOSPI first passed 2,000 in 2007, but it
took over 3 years to get back to 2,000.

26
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:29,588
After that, until 2016, it sat between
1,900 and the low 2,000s for over 6 years.

27
00:01:29,968 --> 00:01:32,072
Hence "Bakseupi": the
index stuck in a box.

28
00:01:32,452 --> 00:01:37,969
Meanwhile, the S&P 500, bundling
America's 500 top companies, rose 81%.

29
00:01:38,349 --> 00:01:40,154
Korean stocks didn't always lose.

30
00:01:40,534 --> 00:01:45,044
KOSPI passed 4,000 last fall, and
this June it climbed to 9,000.

31
00:01:45,424 --> 00:01:51,011
US stocks also fell over 20% in 2022,
and there's exchange-rate risk too.

32
00:01:51,391 --> 00:01:54,225
Still, to avoid piling into
one country and one industry,

33
00:01:54,225 --> 00:01:55,767
I decided to move to US stocks.

34
00:01:56,147 --> 00:01:58,214
And not into one stock, but the S&P 500,

35
00:01:58,214 --> 00:02:00,747
an index that spreads
money across 500 companies.

36
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:04,777
Second, don't leave the market
just because you lost big.

37
00:02:05,157 --> 00:02:09,247
When people lose big, many call stocks
gambling, sell everything and leave.

38
00:02:09,627 --> 00:02:12,957
Until last week, I only thought
about deleting my stock app.

39
00:02:13,337 --> 00:02:16,512
But the moment you leave, the
loss is locked in forever.

40
00:02:16,892 --> 00:02:20,172
So instead of leaving, I
decided to just stop trading.

41
00:02:20,552 --> 00:02:24,456
I keep the account and buy nothing
new until I finish studying.

42
00:02:24,836 --> 00:02:28,608
In the S&P 500, I looked at
the four big drops since 2000.

43
00:02:28,988 --> 00:02:33,166
I left out dividends and looked at price
only, so the numbers run a bit low.

44
00:02:33,546 --> 00:02:36,475
If I had put in 100,000,000
won at the October 2007 peak,

45
00:02:36,475 --> 00:02:39,816
it would have been about 49,000,000
won at the March 2009 bottom.

46
00:02:40,196 --> 00:02:42,866
If I had left here, that
would have been the end.

47
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:46,716
But if I had stayed, I'd have
100,000,000 won back 4 years later.

48
00:02:47,096 --> 00:02:50,098
Held until now, it would
be about 500,000,000 won.

49
00:02:50,478 --> 00:02:55,227
The dot-com crash, the COVID crash and
the 2022 bear market were all the same.

50
00:02:55,607 --> 00:02:58,657
All four times, those who
stayed got back to the peak.

51
00:02:59,037 --> 00:03:02,213
It took as little as 5 months,
as long as 4 years 3 months.

52
00:03:02,593 --> 00:03:05,853
But this is about an index
spread across 500 companies.

53
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:09,073
A single stock might never recover.

54
00:03:10,073 --> 00:03:14,500
Third, don't just follow stock
news; study the macroeconomy.

55
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:18,570
Macro means big forces, like interest
rates, that move the whole market.

56
00:03:18,950 --> 00:03:21,467
Many investors only watch
stock news and charts.

57
00:03:21,847 --> 00:03:24,157
I only read good news about chip stocks.

58
00:03:24,537 --> 00:03:27,827
But the July crash wasn't
one company's problem.

59
00:03:28,207 --> 00:03:31,367
Money crowded into chips and
leveraged (amplified) products.

60
00:03:31,747 --> 00:03:34,288
Analysts said worries about US rate hikes,

61
00:03:34,288 --> 00:03:37,797
AI profitability and geopolitical
tension all hit at once.

62
00:03:38,177 --> 00:03:42,214
When rates rise, deposits pay better, so
money flowing into stocks tends to shrink.

63
00:03:42,594 --> 00:03:44,359
And when the exchange rate spikes,

64
00:03:44,359 --> 00:03:47,215
foreign investors tend to
sell Korean stocks and leave.

65
00:03:47,595 --> 00:03:49,205
Market debt was a signal too.

66
00:03:49,585 --> 00:03:53,819
Margin loans from brokerages hit
38.6 trillion won on June 24,

67
00:03:53,819 --> 00:03:55,322
the highest this year.

68
00:03:55,702 --> 00:03:58,540
That was six days after
KOSPI first passed 9,000.

69
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:01,220
The whole market was running on debt.

70
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:04,114
So before buying, I'll
check indicators like

71
00:04:04,114 --> 00:04:06,570
the long-short interest
rate gap and bonds.

72
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:09,760
I'm not trying to time my
buying and selling with this.

73
00:04:10,140 --> 00:04:12,890
I'm checking whether I'm
overextending right now.

74
00:04:13,890 --> 00:04:17,327
Fourth, build your own rules
from what you've studied,

75
00:04:17,327 --> 00:04:19,236
and don't be swayed by others.

76
00:04:19,616 --> 00:04:24,118
Many buy stocks heard in paid stock-tip
chat rooms, on YouTube and in group chats.

77
00:04:24,498 --> 00:04:27,442
A "leading room" is a paid
chat room that picks stocks.

78
00:04:27,822 --> 00:04:29,275
I paid for one for 2 years,

79
00:04:29,275 --> 00:04:33,473
and this June I even borrowed after
seeing profit screenshots in a group chat.

80
00:04:33,853 --> 00:04:35,513
And I wasn't the only one.

81
00:04:35,893 --> 00:04:38,645
In June and July, the top
net buy of "seohak ants",

82
00:04:38,645 --> 00:04:40,858
Korean retail investors buying US stocks,

83
00:04:40,858 --> 00:04:43,179
was SOXL, a 3x leveraged
semiconductor ETF.

84
00:04:43,559 --> 00:04:48,679
That ETF fell 48.9% from
late May to July 30.

85
00:04:49,059 --> 00:04:51,892
The Korea Capital Market
Institute blamed frequent

86
00:04:51,892 --> 00:04:54,329
trading and overconfidence
for low returns.

87
00:04:54,709 --> 00:04:59,309
And 62% of individual investors
who started in 2020 lost money.

88
00:04:59,689 --> 00:05:03,053
America's Morningstar also found
fund investors earned 1.2 percentage

89
00:05:03,053 --> 00:05:05,979
points less every year because
of their buy-and-sell timing.

90
00:05:06,359 --> 00:05:08,603
So I wrote my rules in a notebook.

91
00:05:08,983 --> 00:05:09,983
No borrowing,

92
00:05:10,363 --> 00:05:13,200
No more than 10% of my
account in one stock,

93
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:17,915
And before buying, write my reasons in
three lines. That's my idea for now.

94
00:05:18,295 --> 00:05:22,383
If I can't write those three lines for a
stock someone recommends, I don't buy it.

95
00:05:22,763 --> 00:05:26,723
With rules, profit screenshots
from others sway me less.

96
00:05:27,103 --> 00:05:30,156
If it doesn't fit my rules, I just pass.

97
00:05:31,156 --> 00:05:35,426
Fifth, make slow profits while
cutting risk as much as possible.

98
00:05:35,806 --> 00:05:40,336
Many people rush to make up losses and
go back to leverage and all-in bets.

99
00:05:40,716 --> 00:05:42,346
I feel that pull most.

100
00:05:42,726 --> 00:05:46,924
So the day after payday, I
only buy within a set amount.

101
00:05:47,304 --> 00:05:48,761
I calculated with the S&P 500:

102
00:05:48,761 --> 00:05:51,723
1,000,000 won a month for 10
years, what would have happened?

103
00:05:52,103 --> 00:05:56,703
I looked at 202 start months,
any month between 2000 and 2016.

104
00:05:57,083 --> 00:05:59,503
Only 8 ended in a loss.

105
00:05:59,883 --> 00:06:03,913
That means in 194 of 202, I
ended up with more than I put in.

106
00:06:04,293 --> 00:06:07,431
The average multiple was
1.6 times what I put in.

107
00:06:07,811 --> 00:06:11,001
Even in the worst case, it
was 0.95 times what I put in.

108
00:06:11,381 --> 00:06:14,043
Of course, past results
don't guarantee the future.

109
00:06:14,423 --> 00:06:17,985
On the other hand, trying to
catch up fast with 3x leverage

110
00:06:17,985 --> 00:06:21,003
would have meant a 76.7%
drop in March 2020 alone.

111
00:06:21,383 --> 00:06:23,728
Rush ahead, and you may never arrive.

112
00:06:24,108 --> 00:06:26,544
I believe that if I
keep building up slowly,

113
00:06:26,544 --> 00:06:28,758
I can get back the money I lost someday.

114
00:06:29,758 --> 00:06:32,190
Even after losing everything
I owned in stocks,

115
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:34,778
I believe it isn't a real
loss if I don't give up.

116
00:06:35,158 --> 00:06:40,407
From today, I'll pause trading and
try to follow the methods I mentioned.

117
00:06:40,787 --> 00:06:43,256
I hope your investing goes well too.

118
00:06:43,636 --> 00:06:45,166
Thank you for watching.
